# Semgrep scan exclusions for the SecForge SAST gate.
#
# NOTE: a project .semgrepignore replaces Semgrep's built-in default
# ignore list, so the standard heavy / build-artifact paths are repeated
# here. (Git-ignored paths are skipped separately by Semgrep regardless.)

node_modules/
dist/
build/
.venv/
vendor/
*.min.js

# --- Vendored upstream manifests ---
# The Keycloak Operator install bundle (CRDs + operator Deployment) is
# generated by the upstream Keycloak project — see the quarkus build
# annotations in operator.yaml — not authored here. The SAST gate exists
# to scan SecForge-authored code; scanning vendored third-party manifests
# only produces findings we cannot action without forking upstream, and
# pod-security on those workloads is enforced at admission by Kyverno
# (require-run-as-nonroot, pss-baseline) regardless of the manifest text.
platform/manifests/keycloak/operator/
